    {
      "source_number": "199",
      "independent_solution": "a: 7/12=0.583333... . Round to n decimal places: x1=0.6,x2=0.58,x3=0.583,x10=0.5833333333. For n>=2 the next digit is 3 so truncation and rounding agree, and successive terms strictly increase; x1>x2 while x2<x3, so the entire sequence is neither increasing nor decreasing. There are no equal terms: all n>=2 are distinct and less than 0.584, hence also distinct from x1. b: 23/45=0.511111... . y1=0.5,y2=0.51,y3=0.511, generally append another 1; y(n+1)-yn=10^(-(n+1))>0. y10=0.5111111111, uniquely. Thus y is strictly increasing."
    },
